-- title:
--   Smooth-point charts on the Igusa ∞-component, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'\ge 1$ is an integer with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the set of non-units of $A$; $\kappa$ denotes the residue field `ResidueField A`. Two function fields occur. The field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the compositum of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions) inside the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, obtained by coefficientwise embedding; the field `fieldBar q M'` is the analogous compositum of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Over $\kappa$ the corresponding reduced fields are `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, the subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated by the reductions of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j(q^{M'})$, and $\bar F :=$ `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring; `ord`, `evalAt`, `IsRational` and `toValuationSubring` are its order function, its $K$-valued evaluation map (defined through the inverse of $K\to$ residue field), the rationality of its residue field over $K$, and its underlying valuation subring.
--
--   The data are: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` with `hW` asserting that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. the set of places $w$ which are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value at the generator `jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; an inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into `fieldBar q M'`; a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisor pushforward, together with the requirements that a constant lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it lies in $A$, that residues of constants are their residues in $\kappa$, and that every non-zero element can be scaled by a constant to have non-zero residue; the hypothesis `hR₀` that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; an index $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a family `OIg` of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) =$ [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21); and a family `OSS` of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, that $f$ lies in `OIg (lineInfty q)` (with `lineInfty q` the point $[1:0]$) precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of non-zero reduction and $f\cdot y = x$ in the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, that every $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ is of the form `redQ q γ • lineInfty q` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg ℓ` the pullback of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of `OIg`; and `hIg_perm`, that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family `OIg`.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that a constant lies in `OSS s` exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the coefficient-embedded $q$-expansion $\bar j$ of $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s`, and moreover for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in `OSS s` and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each `OSS s` is invariant under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each `OSS s` contains an element $t$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of `OSS s` for every $a\in A$.
--
--   Finally there are a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $\bar F$ — the same data as a constant reduction except for the place map and the two divisor clauses — with `hR` asserting $R.\mathrm{integers} =$ `OIg (lineInfty q)` and `hR₀O` asserting that $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OIg (lineInfty q)`; and an element $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a finite set $N$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$, of a subring $S_Q$ of `fieldBar q M'` for every place $Q$ of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$, of ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q\colon A[X]\to S_Q$ and $\chi_{0,Q}\colon S_Q\to\kappa$, and of a set $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that the following hold.
--
--   (1) $|N| = |W|$.
--
--   (2) For every $Q\notin N$, fourteen conditions: the image of every $a\in A$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth; $\varphi_Q$ is formally unramified; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ equals the image of $a$ in `fieldBar q M'` for every $a\in A$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X))=0$; for every $c\in A$ with zero residue there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi\colon S_Q\to A$ with $\chi(\varphi_Q(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A$, with residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ for all $f\in S_Q$, and with $\chi(\varphi_Q(X))=c$; every $f\in S_Q$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there of that element is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; $\varphi_Q(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $Q$-order $1$; $D_Q$ consists exactly of the places $P$ which are rational, for which every $f\in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and for which the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ if and only if $\chi_{0,Q}(f)=0$; every ring homomorphism $\chi\colon S_Q\to A$ fixing the constants and lifting $\chi_{0,Q}$ arises from a unique $P\in D_Q$, in the sense that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f=\chi(f)$ for all $f\in S_Q$; for $P\in D_Q$, an element $f$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ if and only if $f\cdot h = g$ for some $g,h\in S_Q$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h\neq 0$; every non-zero $f$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f=0$ for all $P\in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by the image of a non-zero constant $c\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and every $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $P\in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   (3) For $Q,Q'\notin N$, if some place $P$ belongs to both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ then $Q=Q'$.
--
--   (4) For every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ inside its decomposition group, and every $Q\notin N$: an element $f$ lies in $S_Q$ if and only if its image under the coefficientwise action [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) lies in $S_Q$, and $\chi_{0,Q}$ takes the same value on $f$ and on that image.
--
--   (5) There is a ring homomorphism $j\colon$ `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` $\to\bar F$ such that for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue $j(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$, and such that $Q\in N$ if and only if there is $s\in W$ with: $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ exactly when $j(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$.
--
--   (6) For every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every hypothesis that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residual automorphism `R.resAut τ` preserves $N$: $\tau\cdot Q\in N$ if and only if $Q\in N$.
--
--   (7) For the same $\tau$ and for $Q\notin N$, `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (Dx Q)`, the set of places $P$ with $\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D_Q$, equals $D_{\tau\cdot Q}$ for the residual action of $\tau$ on $Q$.
--
--   (8) For every $g$ in that same subgroup whose pullback moves `OIg (lineInfty q)`, i.e. with $g^{*}\,$`OIg (lineInfty q)` $\neq$ `OIg (lineInfty q)`, and for $Q,Q'\notin N$ and $P\in D_Q$, the translate $g\cdot P$ does not lie in $D_{Q'}$.
--
--   (9) For $Q\notin N$, $P\in D_Q$ and $s\in W$, it is not the case that both of the following hold: the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the coefficient-embedded $q$-expansion of $j$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and, for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at `jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'`, the difference of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that element and $a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$; and the same two statements with the $q$-expansion of $j$ replaced by `qExpand ℚ M' jq` and `jGeomGen` replaced by `jNGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'`.
--
--   (10) For every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: if for no $s\in W$ the condition holds that for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ regular wherever the $q$-expansion of $j$ is regular and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that residue, the difference of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$, then there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $Q\notin N$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ • P ∈ Dx Q`.
--
--   (11) There is a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose valuation subring is `qIntegersBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')`, the subring of elements of non-negative Laurent-series order, and a $Q\notin N$ with $P\in D_Q$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ instance of the construction of the smooth-point charts on the Igusa component of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ at a place above $q$: off a finite set of nodes, in bijection with the supersingular places of level $M'$, each direction of the Gauss ring at $\infty$ carries a formally smooth chart $A[X]\to S_Q$ with its residue disc $D_Q$, the whole family being equivariant for inertia at $q$ and for the level automorphisms, and covering all places that do not specialise into the supersingular locus. It is used in the construction of the Igusa nodes and the associated family of residue discs, and thereby in the semistable-covering input to level lowering at $q=3$.
